    <summary>Tera Term is free software terminal emulator supporting ssh, telnet and serial connection.</summary>
    <description>
Tera Term is free software terminal emulator which supports:

 * TCP/IP (telnet, ssh, raw), serial, and named-pipe connections.
 * VT100 emulation and selected VT200/300/400/500 emulation.
 * Tek4010 emulation.
 * File transfer protocols (Kermit, XMODEM, YMODEM, ZMODEM, B-PLUS, and Quick-VAN)
 * Scripts using the "Tera Term Language".
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>
## Tera Term
### 2026.01.21 (Ver 5.5.2)
  * Bug fixes
    * Fixed text was not rendered correctly when setting character space and Drawing resized font to fit cell width is on. (issue #1006)
    * Fixed an issue where the "Space between characters (lines)" from "Additional settings > Font" tab. This bug was introduced in 5.0. (issue #1008)
    * Fixed an issue where the window was not hidden when ttermpro.exe was launched with the /V option. This bug was introduced in 5.4.1. (issue #975)
    * Fixed an issue where the macro command "connect" failed to connect to the host when ttermpro.exe was launched with the /I option. This bug was introduced in 5.4.1. (issue #975)
    * Fixed sending data using send, sendln, sendbinary, sendtext macro commands follows local echo settings. This bug was introduced in 5.0. (issue #147)
  * Misc
    * Upgraded TTSSH to 3.5.2.
    * Upgraded Inno Setup that is used for the installer to 6.7.0. (issue #963)
    * Upgraded TTX KanjiMenu Plug-in to 0.1.11

## TTSSH
### 2026.01.21 (Ver 3.5.2)
  * Bug fixes
    * Fixed an issue where SCP receiving did not save to the Downloads folder if the receiving folder was not specified. This bug was introduced in 3.1 (Tera Term 5.1). (issue #1057)
    *Fixed an issue that caused a crash when key exchange negotiation failed. This bug was introduced in 3.5.0 (Tera Term 5.5.0). (issue #1070)
    *Fixed an issue where the SCP receiving dialog title was "SCP sending file." (issue #1055)

## TTSSH
### 2026.01.21 (Ver 0.1.11)
  * Modify version information.
    </releaseNotes>
